<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - October statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - October statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production in October 1996 and consumption, imports and exports of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in January/October 1996 compared with 1995 were as follows, said the Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p>    METAL	     PRODUCTION (OCT)    CONSUMPTION (JAN/OCT)</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  100,900    101,900	 574,563    431,971</p>
<p> Lead			 0	1,006	     n/a     58,384</p>
<p> Copper		15,376     15,903	 185,972    173,800</p>
<p> Tin		    1,557	1,498	   5,381	5,035</p>
<p> Magnesium		n/a	  n/a	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,393	1,190	  16,491     15,940</p>
<p> Zinc		  14,010     17,414	 109,271    154,858</p>
<p> METAL		   EXPORTS (JAN/OCT)	IMPORTS (JAN/OCT)</p>
<p>			  1996	 1995	    1996	 1995</p>
<p> Aluminium	  518,670    656,057	  71,203     86,983</p>
<p> Lead		   1,515	2,413	  29,675     45,313</p>
<p> Copper		57,024     52,442	 120,170    139,910</p>
<p> Tin		    9,387	7,972		58	  158</p>
<p> Magnesium	    1,317	  225	   2,097	2,563</p>
<p> Nickel		 4,761	3,960	   8,132	6,836</p>
<p> Zinc		  46,490     43,692	   5,155     36,683</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
